# Dense triangle-free local optima requiring a global replacement

**Date:** 2026-10-11  
**Base:** `ab6dd3336f9f8d440f2bada76edb32153391cddc`, state `2026-10-10.audit.234`  
**Target:** independent Level I global population/replacement route  
**Classification:** proved candidate awaiting promotion; regression  
**Level I:** STILL OPEN. The family below is explicitly nonglobal.

## 1. Candidate bridge being tested

```text
triangle-free + full positive core stress + PSD affine kernel
  + full mixed-bar rank + local diameter optimality
  + asymptotically optimal full-source density
  -> exclusion -> Level I
```

This implication is false. The following unbounded full-source family satisfies
every condition before the arrow and has a certified same-cardinality global
replacement. It demonstrates why the remaining argument must use more than
local stiffness and the leading density coefficient. The positive population
reserve for genuine global minimizers is not discarded.

## 2. Full-source construction

For every sufficiently large odd integer q put

\[
a=\frac{\pi}{2q},\qquad
R=\frac1{2\sin(2a)},\qquad
D=\frac1{2\sin a}=2R\cos a.
\]

Take the q vertices of the regular unit-side q-gon centered at zero. Set

\[
\lambda=1+q^{-3},\qquad r=R-1-q^{-2},\qquad
m=\left\lfloor\frac{\pi r^2}{a_0\lambda^2}\right\rfloor,
\qquad a_0=\frac{\sqrt3}{2}.
\]

Translation averaging for the unit triangular lattice of covolume a0 supplies
at least m sites in the radius-r/lambda disk. Select exactly m, then scale them
by lambda. The resulting interior cloud lies in B(0,r), has minimum separation
at least lambda>1, and contains no unit contacts. Add it to the q-gon to form
A_q of cardinality n_q=q+m. No asymptotic lattice discrepancy theorem is needed:
we prescribe m by the average rather than assert an exact count at one phase.

Every interior-to-wall distance is at least R-r=1+q^(-2)>1. Also

\[
2R-D=2R(1-\cos a)<1/q<1
\]

for q>=5: use sin(pi/q)>=2/q and 1-cos a<=a^2/2, together with pi<4.
Therefore interior-to-wall distances are at most R+r<2R-1<D, and all
interior-to-interior distances are at most 2r<D. Among the wall vertices, only
adjacent vertices are unit contacts, and the actual diameter pairs join cyclic
indices differing by (q-1)/2. Hence the **entire source** has

```text
C = the unit q-cycle,
H = the q-edge odd diameter cycle,
Q = all q wall vertices,
all m interior points contact-isolated and absent from H.
```

It is triangle-free for q>=5. Every source label is retained in all statements.

## 3. Positive normalized KKT stress

Give every contact multiplier alpha=D^2/q and every diameter multiplier beta=1/q.
Their sums are D^2 and one. The regular wall's contact and diameter Laplacians
act radially, and

\[
D^2\sin^2(2a)=\cos^2 a.
\]

Thus alpha times the contact force equals beta times the diameter force at every
wall vertex. All interior forces are zero. This supplies the full normalized
nonnegative KKT equilibrium, scalar, and tensor identities. Both weights are
strictly positive on their respective full actual graphs.

## 4. PSD stress with the exact affine core kernel

On the wall let Omega=alpha L_C-beta L_H. Its Fourier eigenvalues, for
0<=k<q, are

\[
\ell_k=\frac4q\left[D^2\sin^2(2ka)
-\sin^2\bigl(k\pi/2-ka\bigr)\right].
\]

For odd k this becomes

\[
\ell_k=\frac4q\cos^2(ka)
\left(\frac{\sin^2(ka)}{\sin^2 a}-1\right),
\]

and for even k it becomes

\[
\ell_k=\frac4q\sin^2(ka)
\left(\frac{\cos^2(ka)}{\sin^2 a}-1\right).
\]

Since a<=ka<=pi/2-a for 1<=k<q, all eigenvalues are nonnegative. Equality
occurs only at k=0,1,q-1. These modes are the constant and the two actual wall
coordinate vectors. Consequently

\[
\Omega\succeq0,\qquad
\ker\Omega=\operatorname{span}\{1,P_x,P_y\},\qquad
\operatorname{rank}\Omega=q-3.
\]

Extending Omega to the full source adds one independent zero direction for
every interior isolate. No full-source affine-kernel claim is made. The result
is a statement about this explicit nonglobal family, not a selected canonical
stress theorem for arbitrary global minimizers.

## 5. Full mixed rank and genuine local diameter optimality

Relabel the wall in diameter-cycle order, multiplying original cyclic indices
by (q-1)/2. Diameter bars then join consecutive new indices; contact bars join
indices two steps apart. Every triple of consecutive new indices has bar lengths
D,D,1 and is nondegenerate. Starting with its first bar triangle and adding
successive triangles sharing a full edge produces a rigid spanning chain.
Therefore

\[
\operatorname{rank}R_{C\cup H}=2q-3
\]

on the wall. These are triangles of mixed contact/diameter bars; they are not
unit equilateral triangles.

The wall is locally isolated among configurations satisfying all old contact
lower bounds and all old diameter upper bounds, modulo Euclidean isometries.
Here is a direct proof, without a quoted rigidity implication. Let L_e be the
linearized violation row, with sign negative on contact squared length and
positive on diameter squared length. The strictly positive stress satisfies
`sum_e mu_e L_e=0`. If all L_e(w)<=0, positivity forces every L_e(w)=0;
full mixed rank makes w a Euclidean infinitesimal motion. On the orthogonal
complement S of the three Euclidean motions, compactness of its unit sphere
therefore gives c>0 with `max_e L_e(w)>=c|w|`.

Align any nearby candidate wall by its nearest Euclidean isometry, so its
displacement delta belongs to S. Each exact squared-length violation differs
from L_e(delta) by at most 2|delta|^2. If 0<|delta|<c/2, at least one active
constraint is violated. Thus a sufficiently near feasible wall is isometric
to the original and retains diameter D.

Every nearby full-source configuration of diameter at most D must satisfy
those wall constraints. Consequently **A_q is a local minimum of the complete
diameter problem**, even though its isolates may move freely at the same
diameter. Its core is strictly locally isolated modulo isometry; the full
source is not claimed to be isolated in configuration space.

## 6. Exact surface deficit and asymptotic global comparison

Write Delta=pi/(4a0)=pi/(2sqrt(3)). The exact identities and small-angle estimates

\[
R^2-D^2/4=1/(16\cos^2 a),\qquad
R=D/2+O(D^{-1}),\qquad q=\pi D+O(D^{-1})
\]

give, including the bounded floor error,

\[
n_q=\Delta D^2-c_*D+O(1),\qquad
c_* =\pi(1/a_0-1)=2\Delta(2-\sqrt3)>0.
\]

Thus this triangle-free locally optimal family has the globally optimal leading
density coefficient and has q=Theta(D), n_q=Theta(D^2). Nevertheless its global
population excess is

\[
g_q=n_q-1-\Delta D^2=-c_*D+O(1).
\]

In particular it fails the positive D^(2/3) reserve that the canonical
`C-GLOBAL-POPULATION-EXCESS-ASYMPTOTIC-COEFFICIENT` forces on actual global
minimizers. This failure is not a small numerical rounding effect.

Translation averaging supplies an independent n_q-point triangular-lattice
packing of diameter at most sqrt(n_q/Delta), and

\[
\sqrt{n_q/\Delta}=D-(2-\sqrt3)+O(D^{-1})<D
\]

for all sufficiently large q. This is a strict same-cardinality **whole-source
replacement**, proving A_q is nonglobal. No path keeping the old wall or pins
fixed is required. Since the wall is locally isolated, a sufficiently small
feasible source deformation cannot produce that improvement.

The canonical planar bounds in `docs/problem/literature_baseline.md`, Section
2.2, give sqrt(n/Delta)-1<=D(n)<=sqrt(n/Delta). Accordingly

\[
2-\sqrt3-O(D^{-1})
\le D-D(n_q)\le3-\sqrt3+O(D^{-1}),
\qquad D/D(n_q)\longrightarrow1.
\]

The global optimum remains strictly separated from this local family by a
positive constant in diameter, despite the ratio tending to one. Any reference
replacement improving diameter by at least (2-sqrt(3))/2 must move some label
by at least (2-sqrt(3))/4 under every bijection, since diameter changes by at
most twice the maximum label displacement.

## 7. What this disproves and what remains

This family refutes closure from PSD affine-kernel stress, full core mixed rank,
all-order local diameter minimality, actual odd loaded diameter topology, and
asymptotically optimal full-source density. It also shows why a proof need not
arise from a local path out of the old configuration.

It does **not** refute a theorem combining genuine global optimality with the
positive population reserve. It does not supply triangle-free global minimizers.
The full problem's exact quantifiers are unchanged. The live global obligation
remains to construct a strict sub-D n-point replacement or force a unit triangle
in every sufficiently large globally optimal source, including nonlattice
terminal islands whose population excess is positive.

## 8. Exact finite verification

`research/verify_global_odd_wall_local_optima_2026_10_11.py` uses rational Machin
bounds for pi and alternating Taylor bounds for sine/cosine. It certifies the
positive nonzero Fourier modes and checks the rigid bar-chain witness for
several odd q. The zero modes are exact analytic identities in Section 4,
not conclusions drawn from a numerical interval containing zero.

For selected q it constructs explicit interior lattice clouds and independent
same-cardinality reference packets. Exact integer quadratic forms check the
lattice norms and pair distances; interval radius/diameter bounds certify every
wall-to-interior pair uniformly. The script states the full pair counts covered
by these bounds. It does not infer global optimality from local rank or spectra.

All new claims remain unreviewed candidates/regressions pending an independent
audit. No canonical state or current route prompt is changed.
